      "catalog": {
        "title": "Mail Focus Reader",
        "description": "Create a new private application named \"Mail Focus Reader\". The exact technical Application id is mail_focus_reader.\n\nBuild the shortest complete viable mail reading and triage application, not a Gmail clone. Desktop-first UI: a compact folders/labels list on the left and a message list on the right. Selecting a message replaces the list region with the message detail; an explicit Back action restores the list and preserves the selected folder. Only support read/unread, star/unstar, and archive. Do not add compose/send, OAuth settings, label administration, a local mailbox copy, or dashboard widgets.\n\nThe Application must consume the existing portable capability mail.messages.manage ^1.0.0. It must not implement Gmail API or OAuth, and its semantic Application must not name a package, provider, or skill. Reuse the installed CBS Binding/PackageDelivery and an explicitly attachable reusable Gmail credential owned by the capability/provider plane. Use bounded message summaries and progressive next-page pagination for first paint. Fetch full message content only after selection. Mutations require an explicit user gesture. Show connection status and a clear way to attach an existing Gmail connection.\n\nAcceptance: labels load independently; the first message page performs no N+1 metadata fetch; empty, loading, and error states are visible; detail/back preserves the folder; the result can advance through beta, Trial, and workspace; Applications shows only required permissions. Prefer existing AdaOS components and the minimum number of owned artifacts.",
        "categories": [],
        "tags": []
      },
